      "writtenOn": "2022-04-27T21:14:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe this will become clearer after reading the rest of the CL, but I\u0027m having a hard time parsing this or understanding why it would be set to false. Is the idea to give an extension time to do something after the message is received but before GoodCRC is sent?\n\nWould it be possible to have the common partner code call into the extensions, take the return value of that call, and then use it to decide whether to send GoodCRC itself? That seems like it would make the API between the common code and extensions smaller and more obvious than it is currently.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 96,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 4
      },
      "revId": "d591eb1a129f5114054580677c48f7185549c832",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2945b590_3169c1da",
        "filename": "zephyr/include/emul/tcpc/emul_tcpci_partner_common.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1511343
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-28T17:47:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Main purpose of not sending GoodCRC immediately in the common code is to allow of implementation faulty extensions that in some cases skip GoodCRC.\n\nThe problem with returning if GoodCRC should be send is that, usually extension would like to take some actions before GoodCRC is sent. Replacing `tcpci_emul_partner_msg_status()` with return value will require a mechanism to postpone some extension actions to be performed after GoodCRC.",
      "parentUuid": "afec514c_7bb96cab",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 96,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 4
      },
      "revId": "d591eb1a129f5114054580677c48f7185549c832",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1cd5f390_cfc29793",
        "filename": "zephyr/include/emul/tcpc/emul_tcpci_partner_common.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-28T20:09:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What I was imagining is that the common code, upon receiving a message, would 1) do whatever default message handling it has, 2) call into each of the extensions for additional handling, 3) keep track of or react to the return values of the extensions in some way, and 4) send or not send a GoodCRC based on the return values from the extensions. That would cover the case where the extension wants to do something before sending the GoodCRC.\n\nWhat is the case you\u0027re imagining where the extension would want to do something after sending a GoodCRC?",
      "parentUuid": "2945b590_3169c1da",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 96,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 4
      },
      "revId": "d591eb1a129f5114054580677c48f7185549c832",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6099c78b_88293c37",
        "filename": "zephyr/include/emul/tcpc/emul_tcpci_partner_common.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1511343
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-16T16:23:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In previous comment I made a mistake. Extensions usually would take actions after sending GoodCRC. E.g. source on getting `GET_SOURCE_CAP` message should first send GoodCRC and later send its capabilities.\n\nSending GoodCRC in common code is right think, but to emulate some faulty behavior it is required to do some actions first or don\u0027t send GoodCRC at all. As long as `send_goodcrc` in `tcpci_partner_data` is true, common code is sending GoodCRC right after receiving message. When it is set to false (e.g. by faulty snk extension) it is up to extension to make sure that GoodCRC is send at correct moment.",
      "parentUuid": "1cd5f390_cfc29793",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 96,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 4
      },
      "revId": "d591eb1a129f5114054580677c48f7185549c832",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
